 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? Good to hear from you. A sketch is usually just one character, done very quickly, often just to get an idea down on paper. A study, on the other hand, is fully drawn scene, with multiple characters. Kind of. A sketch is quick and rough, whereas a study is detailed and lovely. I' be happy to help. Would you rather start by sketching the clouds, or inking in the trees and rocks? Start with the key elements. The sun, the horizon, and one bright cloud. Fill in the details around them. Enjoyable way to warm up your drawing muscles.",
